        s9_s1_challenge: "Unreal's default collision physics kills kinetic energy on wall impact. Under jam time constraints, I needed wallrunning that preserved momentum and chained into jumps, without the complexity of a full custom movement state and its replicated physics overhead.",
        s9_s1_solution: "I subclassed <code>UCharacterMovementComponent</code> and overrode <code>OnMovementUpdated</code> to run a wall scan every tick while <code>IsFalling()</code>. The character never leaves the standard falling state. Wallrun physics are applied as velocity corrections: a <strong>Dot Product</strong> validates wall angle, a <strong>Cross Product</strong> finds the forward tangent, and pre-impact speed from <code>OldVelocity</code> is forcefully restored.",
        s9_s2_challenge: "Standard Unreal movement is static on inclines. On top of that, exceeding <code>MaxWalkSpeed</code> violently clamps velocity, killing flow. I needed level geometry to actively dictate pacing while keeping physics parameters data-driven.",
        s9_s2_solution: "I wrote a state-aware Master Speed Manager. For slope physics, the system projects <code>DownVector</code> against <code>FloorNormal</code>. I built a <strong>\"Soft Cap\"</strong> system using <code>FMath::FInterpConstantTo</code> to allow excess momentum to naturally decay.",
        s9_s3_challenge: "Dynamically modifying collision geometry is prone to bugs. Transforming into a larger horse entity inside tight corridors can push players out of bounds or crash the movement state.",
        s9_s3_solution: "I wrote a <strong>predictive spatial validation</strong> system using <code>OverlapBlockingTestByChannel</code>. Transformations are safely denied if clearance is insufficient, and state sanitization prevents conflicting physics states.",
        solution_label: "The Solution",
